---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — masterofsomething.com"
  description="How In Practice Media and the Silas Gmail Helper handle data, including Google user data."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] mb-8">Last updated 27 September 2026.</p>

    <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
      In Practice Media is operated by David Florence in Westminster, Massachusetts. This policy
      covers this website and the <a href="/silas-gmail-helper">Silas Gmail Helper</a>, a private
      single-user application that runs on the operator&rsquo;s own computer.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">This website</h2>
    <p class="my-5">
      This site is a static publication. It does not require an account, does not run advertising,
      and does not sell data. Pages are served through Cloudflare Pages, which processes standard
      request data such as IP address and user agent for delivery and abuse prevention.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">Visitor statistics</h3>
    <p class="my-5">
      To see which articles people read and how they find the site, this site uses
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which runs a
      small script on each page. Cloudflare states that Web Analytics &ldquo;does not collect or use
      your visitors&rsquo; personal data&rdquo; and does not track individual visitors across other
      websites. What we see is aggregate only: counts of page views and visits, which pages were
      read, the sites that linked here, and broad categories such as country, device type and
      browser, plus page-loading speed. We cannot identify you from it, we do not combine it with
      any other data, and we do not share or sell it. This site does not use Google Analytics or any
      advertising tracker.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">Silas Gmail Helper and Google user data</h2>
    <p class="my-5">
      The Silas Gmail Helper is a personal tool used by its author on his own Gmail account. It is
      not offered to other users and has no shared server component.
    </p>
    <ul class="my-5 pl-6 list-disc space-y-2">
      <li>
        <strong>What it accesses.</strong> With the <code>gmail.modify</code> scope it reads message
        metadata and content, lists labels, applies and removes labels, and moves threads to Trash.
        It cannot permanently delete mail and cannot send mail.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Why.</strong> Sorting and triaging the operator&rsquo;s own inbox, and summarising it
        for him in a daily briefing he alone reads.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Where it goes.</strong> Nowhere. Data is fetched over HTTPS from Google&rsquo;s API to
        a single computer, held locally, and never transmitted to any third party, model provider,
        advertiser, or other service. It is not used to train any model.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Credentials.</strong> The OAuth refresh token is stored in a local file on that
        computer and is not committed to source control or shared.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Retention and deletion.</strong> Locally cached mail data is retained only while
        useful to the operator and can be deleted at any time by removing the local files. Access
        can be revoked at any time from the Google Account permissions page, which immediately ends
        all access.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="my-5">
      Use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">
      Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">Contact</h2>
    <p class="my-5">
      Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:djflorence@gmail.com">djflorence@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
